But wait, some beaches do allow dogs all year round. For example, places like California’s beaches have different regulations; some are dog-friendly while others aren't. However, even in those cases, there might be limitations. Dogs might not be allowed near the water or in certain parts of the beach. Also, the presence of wildlife, like seagulls or marine animals, could pose a risk to dogs. Additionally, the sand can be hot, which might be uncomfortable for dogs, especially in summer months.

